/* RPC.c - Remote Administration Protocol (RAP) calls for interrogating LAN Manager servers.
 *
 * Implements the small set of MS-RAP "API" pipe calls (server enumeration, share enumeration,
 * user info) that LanManFS uses to populate the OmniClient browser and discover a user's home
 * share at logon.  Also wraps NetBIOS name-service lookups for master-browser and domain-
 * controller discovery (LM_Boot and Lgn_Logon use RPC_GetDomainController to pick the server
 * they connect to).
 *
 * The RAP pipe (\PIPE\LANMAN) is a NetBIOS-era named-pipe protocol carried over SMB1's
 * Transact - modern Windows still exposes it for backwards compatibility.  External callers ride
 * via LanMan_NameOp / LanMan_Transact (RPC_Transact below).
 */

